    Janitor: liveness-aware idle build-cache reclamation (#298/#299)
    
    The office's only .lake rule was age>=30d, which never fires on the fast
    research cadence; the disk peaked at 94% overnight and was relieved only by a
    manual executive action (records/JANITOR-IDLE-CACHE-RECLAIM-2026-10-20.md, which
    recommended exactly this rule).
    
    Add reclaim-idle-caches: delete a .lake cache only when (a) no live process
    references it or its worktree (path_in_use / /proc), (b) it has been idle for
    >= idle_cache_seconds (default 6h), and (c) its worktree is a git worktree with
    no unpushed commits and no uncommitted changes. Deleting a .lake loses only
    build time (recovery: lake update && lake exe cache get && lake build), never
    data. cycle runs it automatically at high/critical pressure (reclaim_enabled=1,
    idle_cache_enabled=1); each decision is logged with its reason. Smoke test 15
    covers dry-run, a clean idle cache reclaimed, and an unpushed worktree retained.
    
    Live dry-run: 2 idle SoringP1 caches identified (8.6 GB); all AssemblyP1
    worktrees correctly protected (unpushed commits).

